@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Team Role API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Account API Permissioning functionality in relation to Team Roles.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Development Team |
	* I tear down the team roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Role |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Assign team role to team attempt
	Koroneiki teams should not be able to be assigned to team roles on accounts by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I attempt to assign the team with the name "Development Team" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a non permissioned user
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the team with the name "Development Team" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the team role "Default Account Role"
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team"

Scenario: View team role on team attempt
	Koroneiki teams assigned to team roles on accounts should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I assign the team with the name "Development Team" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the team with the name "Development Team" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the team role "Default Account Role"
	And I should be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team" and the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And the team with the name "Development Team" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the team role "Default Account Role" visible to a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove team role from team
	Koroneiki teams should not be able to be removed from team roles on accounts by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
