	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I set the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I set the permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I set the permissions for the team role "Default Account Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I assign the team with the name "Development Team" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a permissioned user
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the team with the name "Development Team" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should have the team role "Default Account Role"
	And I should be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team" and the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |

Scenario: Remove team role from team by permissioned user
	Koroneiki teams should be able to be removed from accounts by permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I set the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I set the permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I set the permissions for the team role "Default Account Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I assign the team with the name "Development Team" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a permissioned user
	| Default Account Role |
	And I remove the team with the name "Development Team" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" from the following roles as a permissioned user
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the team with the name "Development Team" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the team role "Default Account Role"
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team"

Scenario: Assign team role to team attempt by newly non permissioned user
	Koroneiki teams should not be able to be assigned to team roles on accounts by newly non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I set the permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I set the permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I set the permissions for the team role "Default Account Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for a permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" for a permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for the team role "Default Account Role" for a permissioned user
	| Assign Team | true |
	And I attempt to assign the team with the name "Development Team" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles as a non permissioned user
	| Default Account Role |
	Then the team with the name "Development Team" assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive" should not have the team role "Default Account Role"
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team"

